## EXPERIMENTAL
Materials and Reagents. Cucurbit[7]uril (CB[7]), tris(2-carboxyethyl) phosphine (TCEP), glucose, ferrocene monocarboxylic acid (Fc-COOH), mercaptohexanol (MCH), N-(3-Dimethylaminopropyl)-N'-ethylcarbodiimide hydrochloride (EDC), N-Hydroxysulfosuccinimide (NHS) and carcinoembryonic
## Analytical Chemistry
antigen (CEA) were obtained from Sigma (St. Louis, MO). Horseradish peroxidase (HRP) and glucose oxidase (GOx) were purchased from J&K Chemical Technology Co., Ltd. (Beijing, China). Matrix metalloproteinase-2 (MMP-2) and matrix metalloproteinases-7 (MMP-7) were provided by Sino Biological Inc. (Beijing, China). The peptide ( $\mathrm{NH}_{2}$ -KKKPLGVRGCCC-SH) was purchased from Science Peptide Biological Technology Co., Ltd (Shanghai, China).
Apparatus. All electrochemical measurements including cyclic voltammetry (CV) and differential pulse voltammetry (DPV) were measured with CHI 660D electrochemical workstation with a conventional three-electrode system.23 The images of various sizes of PtNPs were performed by transmission electron microscopy (TEM, H600, Hitachi, Japan).
Preparation of CB[7] $@$ PtNPs, Fc-peptide, Fc-HRP and Fc-GOx. The $10\ \mathrm{nm}$ PtNPs in diameter were prepared according to the published literature with slight modification.24 Initially, 1 mL $\mathrm{H}_{2}\mathrm{PtCl}_{6}$ aqueous solution $(1\%,w\slash\nu)$ was added into 40 mL of water and then heated to boiling. Afterwards, $6~\mathrm{mL}$ freshly prepared sodium citrate aqueous $(1\%,w\slash\nu)$ was added rapidly and kept for $120\mathrm{min}$ . When the solution gradually changed from light yellow to black, indicating the formation of PtNPs. The obtained solution was treated with centrifugation, washed three times and then dispersed in $2~\mathrm{mL}$ ultrapure water. After that, $200~\upmu\mathrm{L}$ CB[7] (1 mM) was mixed with the aforementioned PtNPs and shaken for $12\mathrm{~h~}$ . Ultimately, CB[7]@PtNPs was synthesized successfully on account of the strong multivalence interaction between
## Analytical Chemistry
PtNPs and carbonyl groups of CB[7].25,26 For comparison, a sequence of CB[7]@PtNPs complex with various sizes of PtNPs were synthesized.27
The preparation of Fc-peptide was described as follows: first, the peptide was pre-incubated with TCEP for $40\mathrm{min}$ to prevent disulfide formation between peptides. Then, 5 mg Fc-COOH was added into $1.0~\mathrm{mL}$ phosphate buffered solution (PBS, pH 7.0) containing $10~\mathrm{mM}$ NHS and $40~\mathrm{mM}$ EDC and incubated for $^\textrm{\scriptsize1h}$ to activate the COOH groups. Next, $300~\upmu\mathrm{L}$ peptide solution $(10~\upmu\mathrm{M})$ was added and the reaction was kept at $4~{}^{\circ}\mathrm{C}$ overnight to obtain Fc-peptide bioconjugates. The same procedures were employed for the preparation of Fc-HRP and Fc-GOx.
Fabrication of the Electrochemical Biosensor. The cleaned glassy carbon electrode $\left(\mathrm{GCE}\right)^{28}$ was immersed in $\mathrm{HAuCl}_{4}$ $(1\%,w/\nu)$ for electrochemical deposition (depAu) under a potential of $-0.2\mathrm{V}$ for $30{\mathrm{~s}}.$ . Subsequently, $15~\upmu\mathrm{L}$ Fc-peptide solution was dropped on electrode and reacted for overnight at $4~^{\circ}C$ , followed by the incubation of $10~\upmu\mathrm{L}$ blocking agent MCH $(2.0\ \mathrm{mM})$ for $50\ \mathrm{min}$ . After that, the obtained MCH/Fc-peptide/depAu/GCE was incubated with different concentrations of MMP-2 for $50~\mathrm{min}$ at $37~^{\circ}\mathrm{C}$ . In order to form the three-dimensional structure, $15~\upmu\mathrm{L}$ CB[7] $@$ PtNPs, Fc-HRP, CB[7] $@$ PtNPs and Fc-GOx $(15~\upmu\mathrm{M})$ were immobilized onto the electrode in turn and stored at room temperature for $30\mathrm{min}$ .
## RESULTS AND DISCUSSIONS
Characterizations for Different Nanomaterials. The morphologies of PtNPs with four different particle sizes were characterized using TEM, and the results were
